    }
   ],
   "gap": "The thm:p15-os-exponential-exit proof (handbook/annex/p15/optional-stopping-and-random-walks.tex lines 590-603) chooses delta>0 with P(xi_1>=delta)>0 (line 597), which requires ruling out xi_1<=0 a.s. The text argues only the case xi_1>=0 a.s. (lines 593-595), which the proof does not use. The case it does use is dismissed with 'the nonpositive case is analogous' (line 595), a 'similarly' step in an owed proof. Owed: a written argument that E e^{theta_0 xi_1} = 1 with theta_0 < 0 and nonconstant xi_1 excludes xi_1<=0 a.s., so that E_x tau < infinity is fully proved. Three results depend on it: the overshoot integrability E_x e^{theta S_tau} <= e^{theta a} E_x tau (line 628), the exact identity E_x e^{theta_0 S_tau} = e^{theta_0 x} (lines 629-630) and the lower-exit bound. The one-sided bound for the possibly infinite T (lines 635-646) does not depend on it.",
